# {{lb|en|not comparable}} Of a woman, female animal, or couple, in [[expectation]] of giving birth; [[pregnant]].
#: {{ux|en|The '''expecting''' mother is enthusiastic about learning childcare.}}
#: {{ux|en|When is the new couple '''expecting'''?}}
# [[expectant|Expectant]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1850| author=James Fenimore Cooper | title=The Ways of the Hour|page=| passage=Dunscomb was in the sanctum, while a single clerk and three or four clients, countryment of decent exterior and '''very''' expecting countenances, occupied the outer room .}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1862| author=James Anthony Froude | title=History of England from the Fall of Wolsey to the Death of the Spanish Armada|page=419| passage=Parma, unwilling to fight an action which might force France into the field, raised the siege; and Alençon, having strengthened the garrison, thrown in supplies, saved his credit with the Low Countries, and at all events, compromised himself, fell back into his '''expecting''' attitude, waiting for Elizabeth to reward him .}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012| author=K. C. Williams| title=The All In Alchemist|page=| passage="Hello!?!" she said in a very '''expecting''' tone.}}

